# Sentry pipeline integrity: drop rules, size and privacy, init timing, transactions, fixtures

Canonical: `rules/sentry-pipeline-integrity.md`

- Every drop rule has a drop and a keep fixture; never drop an outage class; match the outermost exception.
- Initialise Sentry at import time, never in a worker startup hook; no frame locals; bound size with the SDK wire encoder; guard before_send.
- Transactions bypass beforeSend (use beforeSendTransaction) and carry breadcrumbs, extra, tags, contexts, span query and Referer.
- In-place scrubbers make shared fixtures vacuous (factory per call); SDK global state leaks between tests; never write 'Sentry saw nothing' without Usage Stats by outcome.
